# Post-filter application is dead work at preset >= 7 — measured, gated, landed

date: 2026-08-11
host: Apple M4 Pro (8P + 4E), darwin 25.5.0, 12 logical cores
config: 8-bit 4:2:0, still/allintra (hierarchical_levels=0, intra_period=1), CQP
        qp 40, tiles 0/0, single-threaded, no `-C target-cpu=native`
change: `EncodePipeline::with_recon_output(bool)` (default OFF) + the
        `postfilter_consumed` gate in `encode_frame_420_core`

## The claim

On a still frame whose loop restoration is off — every preset >= 7, since
`seq_tools_for_preset` sets Wiener level 0 there — nothing reads the deblocked
and CDEF-filtered reconstruction. The bitstream is already written; the DPB is
never read because every frame is a key frame at `intra_period <= 1`; the CDEF
*search* (preset <= 6) is not running. The two apply passes exist purely to
materialise `last_recon`. C does not do this work either: its preset-10 profile
contains zero CDEF and zero loop-filter samples while emitting a byte-identical
stream (`encode_gap_attribution_2026-08-07.md` §5).

The 2026-08-07 pass ranked this #4 and then a follow-up REFUTED it
(`recon_lazy_refuted_2026-08-07.meta`) — correctly, for the question it asked:
gated off UNCONDITIONALLY, the passes change bytes on 13 of 36 preset-2/6 cells,
and deleting the pre-CDEF snapshot panics the LR path. What that experiment did
not separate is that ALL of its changed cells are preset <= 6. Split by preset,
the answer flips for the fast half.

## Byte-inertness (the gate)

`tools/byteid_fingerprint.sh`, {64,128,256} x qp{20,40,55} x {gradient,uniform},
same binary with and without the skip:

| preset | cells whose OBU changed |
|---|---|
| 2 | 6/18 |
| 6 | 7/18 |
| 7 | **0/18** |
| 8 | **0/18** |
| 9 | **0/18** |
| 10 | **0/18** |
| 13 | **0/18** |

The p2/p6 rows are the anti-vacuity witness: the same experiment that shows 0/90
at presets 7..13 shows the passes ARE load-bearing below that, so the gate can
fail and the preset split is real, not an artifact of a skip that never fired.

Post-change verification on the landed code:
- `tools/byteid_fingerprint.sh` full default grid (now 32..2048): **168/168
  port == C** (`byteid_fingerprint_2026-08-11.tsv`).
- `tools/decode_gate_grid.sh`: **120/120** aomdec + dav1d OK, 120/120
  byte-identical to C.
- `tools/partial_sb_gate.sh`: **146/146** byte-identical.
- `tools/recon_parity.sh`: **432/432** — the opt-in path still produces the
  decoder-exact recon (this gate now sets `with_recon_output(true)`, and its
  s10 cases prove the flag re-enables the passes).
- `cargo nextest run --workspace`: 1027/1028. The one failure,
  `zenav1-svt-dsp residual::tests::residual_recon_distortion_all_tiers_match_core`,
  is PRE-EXISTING on main (reproduced with these changes stashed) — see the note
  at the end.

## Wall clock

`tools/perf_ab.sh`, 9 interleaved paired rounds per cell, order randomised per
round, one untimed warmup per sample, NEITHER SIDE NICED, both arms the SAME
binary (the candidate arm sets the skip through an env-gated wrapper, so there
is no rebuild difference between arms). Every cell `ident=Y`.

| size | preset | base ms | cand ms | ratio | speedup | [p25, p75] |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 256 | 7 | 6.852 | 6.110 | 0.901 | 1.110x | [0.874, 0.906] |
| 256 | 10 | 2.624 | 1.882 | 0.717 | **1.394x** | [0.714, 0.721] |
| 256 | 13 | 2.628 | 1.907 | 0.720 | **1.389x** | [0.703, 0.729] |
| 512 | 7 | 25.988 | 22.523 | 0.871 | 1.148x | [0.859, 0.874] |
| 512 | 10 | 11.571 | 8.560 | 0.734 | **1.363x** | [0.720, 0.753] |
| 512 | 13 | 11.538 | 8.489 | 0.743 | **1.347x** | [0.727, 0.750] |
| 1024 | 7 | 82.671 | 71.319 | 0.868 | 1.152x | [0.855, 0.873] |
| 1024 | 10 | 42.984 | 31.074 | 0.724 | **1.380x** | [0.713, 0.739] |
| 1024 | 13 | 42.968 | 31.089 | 0.723 | **1.384x** | [0.711, 0.727] |

**Identity control** (the same base binary against itself, same grid, same 9
rounds, run immediately after): ratios **0.992 to 1.018**, i.e. a +-2 % band.
Every cell above is far outside it.

Box state: NOT idle. Another agent held one core at 90-100 % (a `bench_a*`
grid in a different repo) for the whole run, so the absolute ms are inflated;
the paired interleaved ratios and the control band are the metric, and both
arms saw the same load. Preset 7 gains less than 10/13 because CDEF's *search*
is off at 7 but the frame still carries more MD work per pixel, so the fixed
filter cost is a smaller share.

Why p7 < p10/p13: identical absolute saving, larger denominator.

## Where it came from (profile)

`/usr/bin/sample`, 1 ms, 20 s, steady-state warmup loop, self time, port at
512x512 preset 10 before the change:

| leaf | self % |
|---|---|
| `cdef::cdef_filter_block` | 11.10 |
| `encoder::cdef::filter_and_count` | 3.89 |
| `cdef::cdef_find_dir` | 3.64 |
| `encoder::cdef::apply_cdef_frame` | 2.34 |
| **CDEF total** | **20.97** |
| `_xzm_free` + `_xzm_xzone_malloc` | 6.46 |
| `_platform_memmove` + `_platform_memset` | 7.24 |

The measured 1.38x is consistent with removing the CDEF cluster plus the three
whole-frame recon clones (`last_recon`, `last_recon_unfiltered`,
`last_recon_pre_cdef`) that the same change stops making.

## Not fixed, pre-existing: `sse_i32` overflows in the overflow-checked profile

`residual_recon_distortion_all_tiers_match_core` panics at
`crates/svtav1-dsp/src/residual.rs:249` ("attempt to add with overflow"), on
main, with this change stashed. Root cause: the C oracle
(`svt_full_distortion_kernel32_bits_c`, pic_operators.c:86) computes
`(int64_t)coeff[i] - recon_coeff[i]` — the cast promotes the subtraction to
**64-bit** — while both port arms subtract in 32 bits (`(x - y) as i64` in
`sse_i32_core`, `vsubq_s32` in the NEON arm). The test feeds full-range i32, so
the scalar arm traps in the test profile; in release both port arms wrap
identically, so the encoder is self-consistent and real transform coefficients
cannot reach the range. Fixing it exactly means widening the NEON subtract too
(there is no i64x2 multiply in NEON), which is a kernel change with its own
byte gate — deliberately NOT bundled into this commit.
